{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/408635-change-of-power-in-freehold","id":408635,"title":"Change of Power in Freehold","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-16T23:13:34-08:00","id":408635,"title":"Change of Power in Freehold","content":"Topic to discuss the ways the power of Courts can flow in the Freehold. How one Court start to rule? Is the Mien of new ruling Court's Monarch changes? The Freehold Frailty Pledge need to be swear with each change? Freehold Monarchs need to rotate some kind of Regalia marking the ruling one?<br /> <br /> I run a small game, with dozen or so of changelings in new forming Freehold in New England. They divided themselves into 4 Seasonal Courts, with Autumn and Winter having only one member. I assume those changelings automatically becomes Monarchs? They need to make more than just swear the Pledge to the Season for this?<br /> <br /> In our game I want to introduce the Courts on Spring Equinox. Is the scene of Winters King passing Regalia to the Spring Monarch correct one? The thing like this looks? If not - how change in power could look like? Is there Winter need to participate, if the Freehold did not existed in it's time of year?<br /> <br /> How the ruling of particular Season changes the life in Freehold? For example, when the Spring takes rule, does all the changelings under it's rule feel more warmth? They get new bonuses?<br /> <br /> How does the Ruing Courts change works for ideas like Day and Night, or Phases of Moon?<br /> <br /> Thanks for help in advance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T00:52:23-08:00","id":408679,"title":"","content":"The answer it...it depends.<br /> <br /> Some Freeholds have major ceremonies. Some have simple quiet ones. Some have a lot of pledging, others do not. None of those are so overwhelmingly common they are the default...the default is the rotating courts, and everything else is how it is handled in the freehold. There is not really a &quot;wrong&quot; way to go about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Whether the single changelings of a court recieve a crown varies. If the freehold acknowledges them, they more than likley do, but maybe they don&quot;t? Who rules then? What if only one rules the colder months?<br /> <br /> It really depends on how you want it structured. Based on the books it varies everything from highly formal occasions with most of the freehold to literally people look at their calendars, realize the season changed, and just switch which monarch they bug.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T03:05:13-08:00","id":408729,"title":"","content":"Are not the Freehold need a Fealty Pledge from every member to the Ruling Monarch? Or to the Freehold itself? If not, just any changeling that is &quot;in town&quot; is treated as under protection of local Court system? That even if Courtier of Moon comes to Seasonal Freehold, just by the being in place under protection of Seasons, he is treated as he was against the Gentry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://fo